Content and brand

The MIT license above covers the code. It does not cover the following, which
are Copyright (c) 2026 Yūnus Andréasson, all rights reserved:

- The Qamar360 name, logo and icons: assets/logo/; icon.png, icon-mark.png,
  android-icon-*.png, splash-icon*.png and notification-icon.png in
  assets/images/; and web/public/favicon.*, web/public/apple-touch-icon.png
  and web/public/icon-*.png.
- The photographs and stills: assets/images/auth-hero.webp,
  assets/images/guide-*.webp, web/public/images/, web/art/ and the social
  card web/public/og.jpg.
- The written content: the wording of the guides, of the catalog of acts
  with its descriptions and translations, and of the website's pages
  (src/constants/guides.ts, src/constants/sunnah-habits.ts,
  src/constants/curated-stacks.ts, src/constants/exchanges.ts,
  supabase/seeds/catalog.sql, web/src/routes/ and
  web/src/components/story.tsx). The code around that text is MIT.
- The screenshots in .github/readme/.

Third-party material keeps its own license:

- Inter, by The Inter Project Authors, under the SIL Open Font License 1.1
  (web/public/fonts/OFL.txt): assets/fonts/ and
  web/src/fonts/inter-4.1.1.woff2.
- web/src/fonts/honorific.woff2: one glyph cut from Noto Sans Arabic, by The
  Noto Project Authors, under the SIL Open Font License 1.1.
- The moon: NASA Scientific Visualization Studio's CGI Moon Kit, from the
  Lunar Reconnaissance Orbiter, public domain: assets/images/moon/,
  assets/images/moons/ and web/public/moon/.
- The sun: a photograph from NASA's Solar Dynamics Observatory, public
  domain: web/public/sun/.
- The app was scaffolded from Expo's create-expo-app template, MIT,
  Copyright (c) 2015-present 650 Industries, Inc. (aka Expo); what remains
  of it stays under that notice.
